  B5 -- THE MISSING INPUT: the far-field boundary condition on u.
        The static (eta = 0) branch fixes u POINTWISE from the local field: u^2 = 1 - e^(-|a|/a0),
        so u -> 0 as |a| -> 0, which is the isolated-MOND boundary condition and is what the deep-MOND
        asymptotics above assume.  The expanding (eta = 1) plateau fixes u by P_w = 0 instead:
        IC10's own solution has u = 0.492193, 0.536585, 0.570419 at S = 0.10, 0.15, 0.20, and the
        IC4/IC5 witness has u = 2/3.  A galaxy sits inside the eta = 0 plateau and the cosmology inside
        eta = 1; the two are separated by the eta transition, which IC10's own 'What remains' item 1
        says has not been varied.  If u must approach its cosmological value at large r, the static law
        reads that as an external field:
        u_cosmo = 0.492193 (IC10 S=0.10    )  ->  equivalent y_ext = 0.2774, i.e. g_ext = 0.277 a0
        u_cosmo = 0.570419 (IC10 S=0.20    )  ->  equivalent y_ext = 0.3936, i.e. g_ext = 0.394 a0
        u_cosmo = 0.666667 (IC4/IC5 witness)  ->  equivalent y_ext = 0.5878, i.e. g_ext = 0.588 a0
        canonical: 27.0% of the bulgeless SPARC points beyond 2 kpc sit at g_obs < 0.28 a0, i.e. BELOW the smallest such floor
        alt      : 37.6% of the bulgeless SPARC points beyond 2 kpc sit at g_obs < 0.28 a0, i.e. BELOW the smallest such floor
  [FAIL] B5 the galactic branch's far-field boundary condition on u is DETERMINED by the published files (i.e. the eta = 0 static branch and the eta = 1 cosmological branch are matched, so an isolated galaxy's deep-MOND asymptotics is fixed)   (not determined: the static law gives u -> 0, the exhibited cosmological solutions give u = 0.49-0.67 (equivalent to a universal external field 0.28-0.59 a0), and the eta transition between them has not been varied (IC10 'What remains' item 1))

  B6 -- two informational diagnostics (flagged, not scored; both need the frame/branch matching the
        lead has not done, so neither is treated here as a failure of the construction).
        (i) a0 vs the expansion rate ON THE ONE EXHIBITED BRANCH.  With m = h0 = 1, kappa = 6 (IC10's own
            numbers) the witness relation gives a0 = 2.4341 h0 while IC10's solution has
            H_phys = 0.719-0.808 h0, so a0/(cH) = 3.01-3.39.
            observed a0/(cH0) = 0.1430 (canonical) -- the exhibited branch is 22x off.
            observed a0/(cH0) = 0.1722 (alt) -- the exhibited branch is 19x off.
            Lambda and kappa are free OFF that branch, so this is a property of the exhibited solution,
            not a theorem; the lead already labels it 'not a viable cosmology'.
        (ii) G_cos vs G_local.  At eta = 0 the Planck mass is m; on IC10's eta = 1 plateau it is
            m* = m e^(-1/6), a ratio e^(1/6) = 1.1814.  Whether that is a real 18% G_cos/G_N
            shift (BBN allows ~10-20%) depends on the conformal factor e^(2w) that matter carries and on
            the transition; it cannot be settled from the published files and is flagged, not scored.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERDICT
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    The static, weak-field limit of the IC-series IS a genuine AQUAL-type MOND theory:
        div[ mu(|grad Phi|/a0) grad Phi ] = 4 pi G_N rho_b,   mu(y) = 1 - e^-y,   G_N = 1/(8 pi m),
    with Phi = Psi (so lensing and dynamics share one potential), the Newtonian limit at high acceleration
    with the same G that normalises R4 and the tensor sector, the deep-MOND law g = sqrt(g_N a0) with
    coefficient exactly 1.000000 x the action's own a0, and every clock/vacuum term the limit drops below
    2e-5 of the retained ones out to 1 Mpc at the construction's own kappa/m.  The constitutive law
    u^2 = 1 - e^(-|a|/a0) is EXACT on the static branch, and that branch is verified here (A6) to be IC5's
    and IC10's own, not only IC1's.  a0 enters as an input, which the programme's rules permit; what the
    theory supplies is the numerical coefficient 1 in front of it, and that is right.
    Two things it is NOT.  (1) The kernel is the framework's EXPONENTIAL CARRIER -- the kernel the programme
    swapped away from on 2026-09-06 in favour of nu_RAR on the bounded-boost ceiling test; it differs from
    the carried kernel by up to 0.073 dex in the transition and violates its own ceiling ~5x more often on
    the bulgeless SPARC control.  (2) The far-field boundary condition on u is not fixed by the published
    files, and the only values the exhibited cosmological solutions offer would read as a universal external
    field of 0.28-0.59 a0.
  [PASS] VERDICT the IC-series, as published, is a candidate host for this framework's galaxy phenomenology -- its static weak-field limit is MOND, at the action's own a0, with one potential and the measured G   (PASS on the reduction; the two open items above are scored separately as B2b and B5 and are not hidden inside this verdict)

